            <div xml:id="d652">

                <pb facs="0776" n="764" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg764"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841E.00/12: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-08-16T19:00:00+01:00">August 16, 1942—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 16—3:38 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4582. For the Under Secretary. I took up with Eden this morning the problem
                    presented in your telegram No. 3874, August 15, 4 p.m. He was not familiar with
                    the matter but promised to look into it immediately.</p>
                <pb facs="0777" n="765" xml:id="pg765"/>
                <p>He has just told me that an appeal has been filed with the Criminal Court of
                    Appeals for which no date has yet been set and which means that inevitably some
                    weeks will pass before the sentence imposed is carried out. In the interim Eden
                    says he will go into the question fully with the Home Office and the Dominions
                    Office.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
